WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:09.092
[theme music]

00:45.879 --> 00:49.090
[woman 1 gasps]
That cake is so beautiful. It's so pretty.

00:49.674 --> 00:52.177
- Looks like someone's about to propose.
- I know!

00:52.260 --> 00:53.678
[gasps]

00:53.762 --> 00:55.054
[slurping]

00:55.138 --> 00:56.139
[woman 2] Ah…

00:56.222 --> 00:58.224
[gentle music]

01:04.898 --> 01:06.524
- [chef] Hey.
- [thudding]

01:06.608 --> 01:09.069
Hey, man. Not there.

01:09.152 --> 01:10.236
- Not here?
- [chef] No!

01:10.320 --> 01:11.321
Those two.

01:13.740 --> 01:15.992
Oh! Apologies.

01:16.076 --> 01:17.702
[cart rattles]

01:20.497 --> 01:21.915
[nervous chuckle]
Sorry.

01:22.832 --> 01:24.959
- [woman 1] It's not them.
- [woman 2] Wow. How beautiful.

01:25.043 --> 01:26.377
Maybe it's for you.

01:26.461 --> 01:28.922
- [woman 3] It wasn't for her.
- [woman 4] No, it's them over there.

01:29.005 --> 01:32.383
- [man] Let's celebrate.
- It's so pretty. What a lucky girl.

01:33.218 --> 01:35.804
- [woman 1] Look at the ring.
- [woman 2] Beautiful.

01:35.887 --> 01:39.390
Soo-jin, will you marry me?

01:39.474 --> 01:44.354
- [customers cheering]
- Say you will. Say you will.

01:44.437 --> 01:47.941
[Ha-kyung] Marriage always felt
like a natural progression for me.

01:49.317 --> 01:54.447
Just like how the flowers bloom in spring
and the rainy season comes in summer,

01:55.073 --> 01:58.868
it felt natural,
something that would just come.

01:58.952 --> 02:00.495
[reporter] Summer heat is in full swing,

02:00.578 --> 02:03.206
and the rainy season's
just around the corner.

02:03.289 --> 02:05.834
Cloudy skies can be expected
starting this weekend

02:05.917 --> 02:07.252
with some ongoing showers…

02:07.335 --> 02:09.379
[Ha-kyung] However, with climate change

02:09.462 --> 02:12.799
and the growing uncertainty
of weather forecasting nowadays…

02:12.882 --> 02:14.175
[glasses clinking]

02:14.259 --> 02:15.635
Why did they take a risk like that?

02:15.718 --> 02:16.636
Huh?

02:16.719 --> 02:18.638
[woman 1] Wow, that's so sweet.

02:18.721 --> 02:21.891
- [man] So cool.
- Oh, uh, it's noisy in here.

02:21.975 --> 02:23.434
- Should we leave now?
- [man] Very nice.

02:23.518 --> 02:25.228
- [Soo-jin] I love it. Ah!
- Okay.

02:27.772 --> 02:31.651
[Ha-kyung] What really is natural
to us anymore?

02:32.569 --> 02:33.945
[sighs]
No way.

02:34.821 --> 02:36.531
How could it even happen?

02:36.614 --> 02:38.908
Those two are together?

02:39.409 --> 02:41.244
Are you sure you're not confused about it?

02:41.327 --> 02:43.037
I saw it with my own two eyes.

02:43.121 --> 02:46.166
The two of them were driving around
and went in for a drink.

02:46.249 --> 02:47.667
Well, they're on the same team.

02:47.750 --> 02:49.252
Of course, coworkers go for drinks.

02:49.335 --> 02:52.630
Also, what's her name? Jin Ha-kyung.
She's not his type at all.

02:52.714 --> 02:53.923
Same thing with Ha-kyung.

02:54.007 --> 02:56.759
She'd never go for a guy
who is that arrogant and headstrong.

02:56.843 --> 02:58.261
That's what I'm saying.

02:58.344 --> 03:00.847
I just don't think it makes sense
that they would be going out, huh?

03:02.765 --> 03:04.392
[groans]

03:13.234 --> 03:14.777
[sighs]

03:14.861 --> 03:16.446
I'm sure that he's just, uh,

03:16.529 --> 03:18.990
going after her
to get back at me, that bastard.

03:19.073 --> 03:20.617
What?

03:21.200 --> 03:24.579
Si-woo oppa is unpredictable,
but he wouldn't do something like that.

03:26.414 --> 03:27.498
"Oppa"?

03:28.291 --> 03:30.251
You just called that guy your oppa?

03:31.044 --> 03:32.295
[sighs]

03:32.378 --> 03:34.422
I misspoke. I take it back.

03:35.298 --> 03:37.133
Anyway, that's not like Lee Si-woo.

03:38.426 --> 03:41.638
Uh-huh. And I bet
he wouldn't do this either.

03:41.721 --> 03:43.348
Look what he did. What he did here.

03:43.431 --> 03:46.100
- That's because you attacked him first.
- I told you.

03:46.601 --> 03:48.353
Never take his side over mine, didn't I?

03:48.436 --> 03:50.188
[sighs]

03:51.481 --> 03:52.732
[Ki-jun] What? What?

03:52.815 --> 03:54.192
What's on your mind?

03:56.361 --> 03:59.405
[sighs]
I'm saying those two are not dating.

04:00.114 --> 04:03.159
So stop dragging other people
into our relationship, oppa.

04:03.993 --> 04:07.580
- Seriously.
- Come on. He's trying to hurt me.

04:07.664 --> 04:09.457
- [door opens]
- I'm serious! I know!

04:09.540 --> 04:10.458
[door slams]

04:17.924 --> 04:19.300
Uh, in the restaurant--

04:19.384 --> 04:21.511
What should we do this weekend?

04:21.594 --> 04:23.596
- Huh?
- We're off duty.

04:23.680 --> 04:25.139
What do you want to do?

04:25.723 --> 04:27.850
Ah, I don't know.

04:28.768 --> 04:31.229
Hmm, we could see a movie.

04:31.312 --> 04:33.982
Or, uh, that horror one
looked pretty cool, so…

04:35.066 --> 04:36.109
Sure.

04:37.485 --> 04:39.570
Maybe we could drive out to the suburbs.

04:40.238 --> 04:41.656
That sounds good too.

04:41.739 --> 04:43.950
Or do you wanna work out together?

04:44.033 --> 04:45.785
Seems like you like to run too.

04:46.286 --> 04:47.287
Also great.

04:49.205 --> 04:52.875
Or we could just get
some groceries from the market.

04:53.501 --> 04:54.335
Okay.

04:55.753 --> 04:59.507
- You're saying okay to everything.
- Hmm?

04:59.590 --> 05:01.092
You don't sound excited.

05:01.718 --> 05:04.887
You're just saying yes to whatever I say.

05:04.971 --> 05:07.348
That's because everything
really does sound good.

05:08.599 --> 05:10.643
To be honest,
I just like walking together.

05:11.227 --> 05:13.062
Well, I do too, yeah.

05:13.646 --> 05:16.691
But we don't get a lot of days off,
so I want us to do something special.

05:17.275 --> 05:18.484
So what's your preference?

05:19.068 --> 05:20.570
Um…

05:20.653 --> 05:22.488
There are a few options.

05:22.572 --> 05:25.575
I want to go check out one
of those rock and roll bowling places.

05:25.658 --> 05:28.244
And I want to go to Jeju Island for--

05:28.328 --> 05:31.039
Let's forget that. There will be
too many newlyweds there

05:31.122 --> 05:32.165
this time of the year.

05:32.832 --> 05:34.083
What's wrong with newlyweds?

05:34.667 --> 05:35.752
I don't know.

05:36.627 --> 05:37.712
It's suffocating?

05:38.421 --> 05:39.630
What do you mean?

05:39.714 --> 05:44.052
That, uh, whole thing of marriage
being the end goal, it's not always right.

05:44.135 --> 05:48.473
When I see married people acting
like now, it's all happily ever after.

05:51.267 --> 05:53.061
Well, it's different for everyone.

05:53.644 --> 05:56.481
But still, I just feel
a little suffocated.

05:59.442 --> 06:02.028
Oh, hang here.
I'll go get us some cold drinks.

06:02.111 --> 06:04.322
- Hmm.
- Okay.

06:05.573 --> 06:07.950
[pensive music]

06:14.832 --> 06:20.421
EPISODE 9
DRY CHANGMA (RAINY SEASON)

06:20.505 --> 06:23.174
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

06:26.219 --> 06:29.180
A stationary front has currently formed
over the southern Jeju Sea.

06:29.263 --> 06:32.433
It seems like it will start raining
in Jeju early tomorrow now.

06:33.434 --> 06:38.564
The stationary front is moving
along about how we expected at 35km/h.

06:39.857 --> 06:41.317
- Thirty-five kilometers?
- Yes.

06:42.944 --> 06:45.905
[Bong-chan] Judging
by the current situation in the air,

06:45.988 --> 06:49.575
rainfall will start in the metro area
tomorrow evening as expected.

06:49.659 --> 06:51.744
- [Ha-kyung] That's right, sir.
- [Bong-chan] Hmm.

06:53.204 --> 06:55.248
- How about the press?
- Uh, yes.

06:55.331 --> 06:56.833
Because of the heat wave,

06:56.916 --> 06:58.835
the rainy season
has everyone very excited.

06:58.918 --> 06:59.877
I see.

07:00.628 --> 07:01.879
Okay, good.

07:01.963 --> 07:05.049
We'll give the press the briefing
as planned. Let's move on.

07:05.133 --> 07:07.969
Yes, sir. Hello, Jeju Office?

07:08.052 --> 07:10.805
[light music]

07:10.888 --> 07:12.348
[Bong-chan] All right.

07:12.431 --> 07:13.641
Great job, everyone.

07:13.724 --> 07:15.726
[all] Thank you!

07:15.810 --> 07:18.896
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

07:28.990 --> 07:30.158
May I have a word with you?

07:32.827 --> 07:33.828
[sighs]

07:47.800 --> 07:49.177
Are you dating Lee Si-woo?

07:51.095 --> 07:52.054
What?

07:52.763 --> 07:53.848
Am I dating who?

07:53.931 --> 07:55.892
I saw everything. I saw you together.

07:56.767 --> 07:59.520
The place I told you
that's a good spot to go have a drink.

07:59.604 --> 08:01.230
The Izakaya, I saw you two.

08:01.314 --> 08:03.483
[comical music]

08:03.566 --> 08:05.318
Ah, that night.

08:06.027 --> 08:08.112
[chuckles]
Lee Si-woo and I are teammates.

08:08.196 --> 08:09.989
Can't a couple of teammates
go for a drink?

08:10.072 --> 08:11.991
- That looks like dating to you, huh?
- Nu-uh.

08:12.492 --> 08:15.119
Your mouth on his
is what looks like dating.

08:16.704 --> 08:18.122
[laughs]
What? Come on!

08:18.206 --> 08:21.542
[sighs]
You've really changed, Jin Ha-kyung.

08:21.626 --> 08:24.754
When we dated, you used to hate showing
any affection when others were around.

08:24.837 --> 08:27.381
And now you're out there going around
kissing Lee Si-woo

08:27.465 --> 08:28.716
where the whole bar can see you.

08:30.927 --> 08:33.846
You… I should have known since that day.

08:34.430 --> 08:36.098
When I was fighting with him,

08:37.058 --> 08:40.394
I thought it was weird you left together,
so I followed to see where you went.

08:40.478 --> 08:42.188
You were having a real moment.

08:42.271 --> 08:43.397
[scoffs]
Then…

08:43.898 --> 08:44.941
Am I supposed to do nothing

08:45.024 --> 08:46.817
if my subordinates get beat up
by some psycho?

08:46.901 --> 08:49.862
A psycho who I was involved with
in the past?

08:49.946 --> 08:51.280
- "Psycho"?
- What of it, huh?

08:51.364 --> 08:53.366
Why would I ever want to date
in the workplace again

08:53.449 --> 08:55.868
after what you and I went through?
Are you crazy?

08:56.452 --> 08:57.954
- What--
- [Ha-kyung] Also…

08:59.497 --> 09:02.750
Why do you even care
who I'm kissing or making out with?

09:02.833 --> 09:03.709
[sighs]

09:03.793 --> 09:04.961
- Hey!
- What?

09:05.962 --> 09:07.171
I'm scared for you, 'kay?

09:08.005 --> 09:09.632
Men know what men can do.

09:09.715 --> 09:12.218
Lee Si-woo is not a decent guy.

09:12.301 --> 09:15.179
Also, I didn't want to bring this up.

09:15.263 --> 09:18.349
But do you even know what kind of scene
he made at my wedding with Yu-jin?

09:18.432 --> 09:21.686
Ah, so you broke off our wedding
with everything planned

09:21.769 --> 09:23.980
to marry another woman
because you're such a good guy?

09:24.063 --> 09:27.024
Oh, gosh, look, okay?
Yu-jin gave me no choice.

09:27.108 --> 09:29.694
That bastard is just trying to get
his revenge on me through you.

09:29.777 --> 09:32.071
Oh, so you're just really concerned,
then, huh?

09:32.154 --> 09:33.406
Of course, I'm concerned.

09:33.489 --> 09:35.616
The only thing you're scared off
is your name getting dragged

09:35.700 --> 09:37.660
through the dirt
if I go out with Lee Si-woo.

09:37.743 --> 09:39.912
Well, of course, yeah, that too.

09:39.996 --> 09:41.831
Be honest. Wouldn't you be scared of that?

09:43.541 --> 09:44.834
- Hey!
- What?

09:44.917 --> 09:46.002
Go to hell.

09:46.085 --> 09:49.672
[comical music]

09:51.257 --> 09:53.175
Ha-kyung, you can't do this!

09:53.259 --> 09:54.760
Ha-kyung, hey!

09:56.304 --> 09:59.223
[sighs]
She's got no sense at all.

10:01.267 --> 10:02.435
[inhales deeply]

10:04.687 --> 10:06.772
[tense music]

10:07.648 --> 10:08.899
[sighs]

10:14.655 --> 10:17.158
It's revenge! I'm serious!

10:17.241 --> 10:18.868
[groans]

10:22.955 --> 10:24.957
[playful music]

10:33.966 --> 10:35.343
[grunts]

10:35.426 --> 10:38.554
[humming gleefully]

10:40.556 --> 10:43.851
[chuckles, taps]
Aren't you excited for the weekend, huh?

10:44.435 --> 10:47.730
Of course.
It's my first weekend in forever.

10:47.813 --> 10:50.775
I can't ever see anybody
on a weekday when I'm off.

10:50.858 --> 10:52.526
It's so lonely.

10:53.277 --> 10:54.111
[sighs]

10:54.195 --> 10:56.614
I wish I could have
a little loneliness on my day off.

10:56.697 --> 10:59.825
Just kids. Kids all the time,
whenever I get a weekend.

10:59.909 --> 11:01.369
And if they've got study sessions,

11:01.452 --> 11:03.746
I have to take them back
and forth all over town.

11:04.330 --> 11:05.623
I'd rather be right here.

11:06.374 --> 11:07.375
Mm.

11:10.836 --> 11:13.381
I already know what Mr. Um's gonna do.

11:16.342 --> 11:18.386
What are you doing tomorrow, Mr. Lee?

11:19.011 --> 11:20.971
I've got a date, so…

11:21.055 --> 11:22.932
[Si-woo] I heard that a good play opened.

11:23.015 --> 11:25.309
Oh, I love theater. What show is it?

11:25.393 --> 11:27.686
Oh, uh… What was it?

11:27.770 --> 11:28.604
[message received tone]

11:28.687 --> 11:31.023
- [Ha-kyung] Emergency.
- "Emergency"?

11:31.107 --> 11:32.400
[Soo-jin] "Emergency"?

11:32.983 --> 11:34.693
- Oh, the show?
- Huh?

11:34.777 --> 11:37.488
Oh, uh, it's a musical at a small theater.

11:37.571 --> 11:39.115
Oh, a small theater.

11:39.198 --> 11:41.033
- [keyboard clacking]
- [Si-woo] What is it?

11:42.368 --> 11:44.203
And you, Mr. Shin? Your weekend?

11:44.286 --> 11:47.248
Well, a weekend off
doesn't change anything.

11:47.957 --> 11:51.335
- First, when I get up, I make a coffee.
- [Soo-jin] Hmm.

11:51.419 --> 11:53.337
[Ha-kyung] Han Ki-jun is onto us.

11:55.172 --> 11:56.132
[Si-woo] How?

11:56.841 --> 11:59.844
[Ha-kyung] He saw us together
at the Izakaya that day.

12:01.345 --> 12:03.180
[Si-woo] So what did you say?

12:03.264 --> 12:04.515
[indistinct chatter]

12:04.598 --> 12:06.350
[Ha-kyung] I denied it, of course.

12:11.021 --> 12:14.150
[Seok-ho] For breakfast,
I usually have a simple salad.

12:15.192 --> 12:18.654
Work out and try
and clean up around the house.

12:18.737 --> 12:22.741
[Si-woo] Or maybe
why don't we just come clean?

12:22.825 --> 12:24.493
[Ha-kyung] We have to keep denying it.

12:25.619 --> 12:27.329
[Seok-ho] I eat the food when it comes.

12:27.913 --> 12:29.790
And after lunch, I put on a record…

12:29.874 --> 12:32.209
[Ha-kyung] Let's not go
to Daehangno tomorrow.

12:34.587 --> 12:35.921
[Si-woo] Why not?

12:36.005 --> 12:38.632
[Ha-kyung] There's a maeundalgbaljib place
Ki-jun really likes there.

12:38.716 --> 12:42.094
He goes there sometimes,
so I think tomorrow is too risky.

12:42.178 --> 12:44.555
[Seok-ho] …classical pianists have
different brain structures.

12:44.638 --> 12:45.639
Actually…

12:45.723 --> 12:47.516
[Si-woo] It wasn't easy
to get those tickets.

12:47.600 --> 12:49.643
Should we go for a jog near Hangang, then?

12:49.727 --> 12:51.645
[Seok-ho] When they need a jazz pianist…

12:51.729 --> 12:54.940
[Ha-kyung] No. We shouldn't
go outside at all for a while.

12:55.024 --> 12:56.400
[keyboard clacking]

12:56.484 --> 12:58.319
[Si-woo] We can't just stay home.

12:58.402 --> 12:59.862
[Seok-ho] The biggest difference was that

12:59.945 --> 13:01.822
the jazz pianists showed
high reactive brains

13:01.906 --> 13:04.158
and the classical pianists
showed high accuracy.

13:04.241 --> 13:06.160
- [sighs]
- It's fascinating.

13:06.243 --> 13:10.789
They're both interesting, depending
on the perfect opportunity to focus on.

13:10.873 --> 13:14.001
Their brainwaves have
physical reactions differently.

13:14.084 --> 13:15.878
So maybe it's the same for us?

13:16.504 --> 13:20.382
We're all forecasters,
but for digital forecasters…

13:22.801 --> 13:25.971
CONTINUOUS HEAT WAVE…
JIN HA-KYUNG?

13:26.055 --> 13:29.141
[Ki-jun] Yu-jin, do you know
who Lee Si-woo is dating right now?

13:29.725 --> 13:30.726
Who is he dating?

13:31.310 --> 13:32.394
Jin Ha-kyung.

13:34.313 --> 13:35.940
[sighs]
Makes no sense.

13:36.023 --> 13:38.025
- What?
- Huh?

13:38.108 --> 13:40.653
- [Eun-ji] What makes no sense?
- Nothing, I'm good.

13:42.363 --> 13:43.989
MOTHER-IN-LAW

13:44.615 --> 13:46.700
[phone vibrates]

13:52.831 --> 13:54.959
[vibrating continues]

13:59.255 --> 14:00.673
[deep exhale]

14:02.007 --> 14:04.760
Hi, mother. How are you?

14:04.843 --> 14:06.053
[giggles]

14:07.471 --> 14:08.514
Sorry?

14:09.807 --> 14:13.644
Ah. Oh, so sorry. Um, I forgot.

14:13.727 --> 14:15.813
Uh, yes, I'll tell Ki-jun.

14:17.565 --> 14:18.607
Okay.

14:19.525 --> 14:21.902
Well, I'll see you this weekend.

14:21.986 --> 14:23.153
Yes.

14:28.868 --> 14:30.369
[sighs]

14:38.878 --> 14:41.338
- [Eun-ji] Where are you going?
- Uh, shopping errand.

14:41.422 --> 14:42.339
"Shopping"?

14:43.215 --> 14:45.718
- [elevator dings]
- [automated voice] Door is opening.

14:48.804 --> 14:50.931
[phone vibrates]

14:52.600 --> 14:54.435
- [automated voice] Door is closing.
- Hey, eonni.

14:55.227 --> 14:57.646
[Tae-kyung] Mom said you should drop by
on your way home today.

14:57.730 --> 14:59.189
Um, I'm busy.

15:02.192 --> 15:05.362
She's going to go to your place
if you don't come over here.

15:06.322 --> 15:07.823
- I'm sure she will--
- [Dong-han] Si-woo.

15:07.907 --> 15:09.325
What should we do for dinner?

15:10.034 --> 15:12.912
- Budaejjigae sounds good.
- [Dong-han] You know how to make it?

15:12.995 --> 15:15.456
- Okay. I'll be right there.
- No. I know how to order it, though.

15:17.541 --> 15:21.003
- That's strange.
- What? She's not coming here?

15:22.296 --> 15:24.298
- She's on her way.
- Huh?

15:25.299 --> 15:26.300
Ma.

15:26.383 --> 15:28.093
Are you really gonna confront Ha-kyung?

15:28.177 --> 15:29.219
Just leave her alone.

15:29.303 --> 15:31.639
That is not what parents do.

15:33.057 --> 15:34.141
[sighs]

15:36.060 --> 15:38.646
- [Si-woo] What else should we add?
- [indistinct chatter]

15:38.729 --> 15:40.522
- [Dong-han] Dumplings.
- [Si-woo] Dumplings? All right.

15:40.606 --> 15:42.608
- Yeah, and we have ramen at home.
- We do have ramen.

15:42.691 --> 15:45.945
Ooh, we're gonna order, uh, budaejjigae.
Is there anything we should add to that?

15:46.028 --> 15:49.823
Uh, well, I got to go to my mom's house,
so you two enjoy dinner.

15:50.824 --> 15:51.825
Your mom's?

15:53.410 --> 15:55.454
- Is something, uh…
- I don't know.

16:04.546 --> 16:06.674
You know the school trip
I need for credit?

16:07.508 --> 16:08.926
[Bo-mi] Where should I go this time?

16:10.886 --> 16:11.971
[Hyang-rae] Where are you?

16:12.054 --> 16:13.847
[Dong-han] At the KMA, like always.

16:13.931 --> 16:15.683
He's not here. He left a while ago.

16:18.352 --> 16:20.521
Where on earth
has he been sleeping these days?

16:23.315 --> 16:24.233
Mom?

16:25.985 --> 16:26.860
Huh?

16:27.444 --> 16:29.488
It's okay. I can handle it.

16:29.571 --> 16:31.031
[chuckles]

16:31.115 --> 16:33.158
- What is it?
- The school trip.

16:37.830 --> 16:39.123
I have one idea.

16:42.001 --> 16:44.753
[Soo-ja] Go on just three blind dates
that I arranged.

16:45.421 --> 16:47.715
That's my final wish.

16:47.798 --> 16:50.175
Come on, Ha-kyung. Just do it.

16:51.844 --> 16:53.220
I said no from the start.

16:53.721 --> 16:55.431
Am I supposed to throw away money
for nothing?

16:55.514 --> 16:57.850
What about my time, huh?
Should I throw that out?

16:58.642 --> 17:02.229
That's the reason I said
only three dates and no more.

17:03.522 --> 17:06.400
Who knows? Maybe on one of those,
you'll meet the man for you.

17:06.984 --> 17:10.612
These days, they say couples
who met this way

17:10.696 --> 17:14.324
get divorced far less than those
who just met through dating.

17:15.117 --> 17:17.369
[scoffs]
Why look at me?

17:17.453 --> 17:18.787
[Soo-ja] Passion and drama?

17:18.871 --> 17:21.331
All of that's no good at all.

17:21.415 --> 17:22.833
Just look at Tae-kyung.

17:22.916 --> 17:24.918
They acted like
they'd die without each other,

17:25.002 --> 17:26.503
and then one year
after the wedding, divorce.

17:26.587 --> 17:28.672
Mom, why do you always say that?

17:28.756 --> 17:30.466
It's about her, not me!

17:31.383 --> 17:32.801
[door slides open]

17:34.386 --> 17:37.473
Don't try and wait
to pay me respect once I'm gone.

17:37.556 --> 17:40.559
There's still time for that now, huh?

17:41.685 --> 17:43.020
[Soo-ja] While I'm living.

17:46.857 --> 17:49.693
[playful music]

17:49.777 --> 17:52.404
[crickets chirping]

17:52.988 --> 17:55.532
[Soo-ja] You cold-hearted brat!

17:56.200 --> 17:58.410
It's the last wish
of your old mother, huh?

17:58.494 --> 18:01.830
Is it really that hard?
How can you just say no?

18:01.914 --> 18:03.040
- Listen!
- [banging on table]

18:03.665 --> 18:05.250
How can you just strike me down

18:05.334 --> 18:08.087
without the slightest hesitation, huh?
Huh?

18:08.170 --> 18:11.632
I'm sick of always hearing about marriage.
What? Are they arresting singles?

18:11.715 --> 18:14.051
Oh! Oh! That little…

18:15.344 --> 18:18.138
- I'm leaving.
- You're being too harsh.

18:19.556 --> 18:22.309
You know she's just acting like that
'cause she's frustrated.

18:22.392 --> 18:24.853
You and I are the only kids she has.

18:25.979 --> 18:30.484
Her eldest came crawling to her,
a failed wife, and her youngest…

18:30.567 --> 18:32.069
She just wants to know that

18:32.152 --> 18:34.613
you and I'll have someone to lean on
when she goes.

18:35.531 --> 18:37.533
Come on, that's all she wants.

18:39.785 --> 18:42.037
Well, then, Mom can remarry.
Oh! Or you could.

18:42.121 --> 18:44.706
Hey, watch your manners.

18:46.333 --> 18:48.710
Do you know how I feel
every time it goes like this?

18:49.294 --> 18:51.839
I feel like I'm being pushed
to the edge of a cliff.

18:51.922 --> 18:55.843
And how come it always feels that way?
It makes me feel so angry.

18:57.678 --> 18:59.888
Yeah. You got a point.

19:01.557 --> 19:04.059
Anyway, I… I feel awful. I'm heading out.

19:07.437 --> 19:08.772
[door opens]

19:10.107 --> 19:11.692
[door closes]

19:11.775 --> 19:12.901
[sighs]

19:13.944 --> 19:16.238
[mellow music]

19:23.495 --> 19:24.496
[sharp exhale]

19:24.580 --> 19:28.292
[mellow music]

19:29.126 --> 19:30.169
[Tae-kyung] Ma.

19:32.546 --> 19:34.798
Were you happy
when you and Dad were together?

19:36.341 --> 19:39.094
Why would you go and ask me that
out of nowhere?

19:40.179 --> 19:42.890
There's not one marriage that's just good.

19:42.973 --> 19:45.517
Sometimes it's simple.
And sometimes it's not.

19:46.268 --> 19:51.690
Despite that, two is better than one,
and three is much better than two.

19:51.773 --> 19:52.941
You know Mi-jeong.

19:53.025 --> 19:55.986
Her daughter would use to say
she'd live alone forever.

19:56.069 --> 19:57.487
But look now.

19:57.571 --> 20:00.449
Now she's got a great life.
A husband and kids too.

20:01.158 --> 20:03.243
And her husband's got a good job.

20:04.453 --> 20:05.329
[inhales sharply]

20:05.412 --> 20:08.665
But you have to understand
Ha-kyung's not the same as her.

20:10.292 --> 20:11.919
Maybe living alone really works for her.

20:12.502 --> 20:13.337
What?

20:15.380 --> 20:18.258
Well, it's worth considering at least.

20:20.302 --> 20:24.181
Go to bed. All that yelling this evening
must have tired you out.

20:25.599 --> 20:26.600
[grunts]

20:31.521 --> 20:33.523
[mellow music]

20:36.568 --> 20:37.653
Oh, hey.

20:39.655 --> 20:40.739
Hey.

20:42.074 --> 20:43.325
Your mom called today.

20:46.745 --> 20:48.872
She wants to have dinner with us tomorrow.

20:49.498 --> 20:50.874
You're free, aren't you?

20:52.501 --> 20:53.919
Did you go shopping again?

20:55.128 --> 20:57.673
- Oh, uh, that's--
- Must be nice to be so carefree.

20:57.756 --> 21:00.008
I thought we were saving money
'cause of our lease.

21:01.176 --> 21:04.054
We can afford the deposit
for the new place thanks to the loan.

21:04.137 --> 21:07.057
But you know it's not cheap to move
and there's still a lot to take care of.

21:07.140 --> 21:10.769
Are you saying that I'm just
thoughtlessly spending our money?

21:11.728 --> 21:12.938
If you were being rational,

21:13.522 --> 21:15.732
you wouldn't have spent
our money like it's nothing.

21:15.816 --> 21:16.733
Oppa.

21:16.817 --> 21:18.110
Forget about it.

21:18.193 --> 21:19.861
It'll just become a fight if we talk.

21:20.988 --> 21:22.239
I gotta shower.

21:24.449 --> 21:26.118
- [door opens]
- [sighs]

21:26.910 --> 21:27.828
[door closes]

21:33.208 --> 21:34.376
[sighs]

21:36.128 --> 21:37.587
[phone vibrates]

21:42.801 --> 21:44.344
[Si-woo] Is something going on at home?

21:45.304 --> 21:47.306
[gentle music]

21:50.475 --> 21:51.727
[Ha-kyung] Yeah.

21:51.810 --> 21:54.146
But you don't have to worry about it.

21:58.984 --> 22:00.319
[Si-woo] If you're tired,

22:00.402 --> 22:03.363
I'm fine with just chilling
at the apartment tomorrow.

22:09.536 --> 22:11.955
Will you look out the living room
in a second?

22:20.172 --> 22:21.131
Want a beer?

22:23.675 --> 22:25.344
[comical music]

22:25.427 --> 22:27.721
Uh, no, all for you.

22:27.804 --> 22:29.556
- [chuckles]
- Mm-hmm.

22:33.185 --> 22:34.895
[sighs]

22:36.938 --> 22:38.231
[grunts]

22:39.649 --> 22:41.151
[sucks teeth]

22:42.277 --> 22:45.155
[Si-woo] Yeah, staying here
is not really an option.

22:45.238 --> 22:46.281
Is it?

22:46.364 --> 22:48.825
[Ha-kyung] Let's just avoid
crowded places.

22:50.660 --> 22:53.538
A place where it's less crowded
when it rains.

22:53.622 --> 22:55.373
Can you think of a place like that?

22:58.418 --> 23:01.046
[Si-woo] There is one place
I can think of.

23:02.089 --> 23:04.508
- [Ha-kyung] Where?
- [Si-woo] Do you like nature?

23:05.467 --> 23:06.676
[Ha-kyung] Of course.

23:08.345 --> 23:10.514
[Si-woo] Can you stand
a little inconvenience?

23:14.518 --> 23:15.977
[Ha-kyung] I guess.

23:16.812 --> 23:17.979
[Si-woo] Okay, then.

23:21.441 --> 23:24.319
Where are we going?
[chuckles]

23:35.038 --> 23:36.498
[exhales]

23:45.340 --> 23:46.591
[giggles]

23:46.675 --> 23:49.010
What are you doing, huh?

23:54.558 --> 23:56.601
[playful music]

24:11.575 --> 24:13.243
[car engine shuts off]

24:17.205 --> 24:18.915
[Ki-jun] You're off work today, right?

24:18.999 --> 24:20.458
I need to talk to you.

24:20.542 --> 24:22.878
Meet me at the brunch café
in front of the apartment when you get up.

24:22.961 --> 24:24.171
I'll be waiting.

24:26.173 --> 24:27.632
[sighs]

24:30.302 --> 24:32.304
[birds chirping]

24:34.598 --> 24:36.224
Hmm?

24:43.648 --> 24:46.902
[mischievous music]

24:47.569 --> 24:48.737
Morning.

24:48.820 --> 24:50.614
- Lee Si-woo.
- [car door closes]

24:50.697 --> 24:52.324
- [Ha-kyung] Thanks for waiting
- Shall we?

24:52.407 --> 24:54.993
What? Director and subordinate together?

24:57.329 --> 24:59.289
You two are busted.

25:01.541 --> 25:03.376
[engine starts]

25:06.254 --> 25:07.839
[engine starts]

25:16.765 --> 25:19.768
[upbeat music]

25:31.446 --> 25:33.281
Where the hell are they going?

25:36.409 --> 25:37.577
[Ki-jun sighs]

25:41.122 --> 25:42.332
[groans]

25:44.042 --> 25:45.168
[phone vibrates]

25:50.757 --> 25:52.008
HONEY

25:52.092 --> 25:55.136
[Yu-jin] Where are you? You didn't forget
that we're visiting your mom, right?

25:55.220 --> 25:58.223
We need to leave before six,
so be home by then.

25:58.306 --> 26:00.725
- All right. I got time. I got time.
- [phone clacks]

26:03.103 --> 26:04.646
Traffic looks lighter.

26:05.272 --> 26:07.691
- So where are we going?
- We're almost there.

26:09.776 --> 26:12.904
[exhales]
I hope you'll enjoy it.

26:17.284 --> 26:19.286
[chill upbeat music]

26:36.469 --> 26:37.804
- Thank you.
- It's right up there.

26:37.887 --> 26:39.848
- [Si-woo] Thank you.
- You're welcome.

26:39.931 --> 26:41.683
[intriguing music]

26:50.817 --> 26:51.860
[car door opens]

26:52.736 --> 26:54.446
- [splattering]
- What?

26:56.614 --> 26:58.241
[groans]
Who let their dog…

26:59.492 --> 27:01.911
- [Ki-jun] You little…
- [whines]

27:02.495 --> 27:05.373
- Oh, jeez.
- [shoe squeaking]

27:05.457 --> 27:08.626
[phone vibrating]

27:08.710 --> 27:12.297
HONEY

27:12.380 --> 27:14.716
[upbeat music]

27:19.220 --> 27:20.597
This is so nice.

27:20.680 --> 27:22.223
[pants]

27:22.849 --> 27:23.975
[Si-woo] I'm so glad we came here.

27:24.059 --> 27:25.101
Here, I'll help with that.

27:25.185 --> 27:26.519
- [Ki-jun grunts]
- No, it's okay.

27:27.771 --> 27:29.439
[groans]

27:33.610 --> 27:35.904
[moans in pain]

27:37.614 --> 27:40.158
- [sighs]
- [line ringing]

27:40.241 --> 27:42.827
How come he's ghosting me all of a sudden?

27:44.287 --> 27:45.205
[sighs]

27:45.997 --> 27:47.999
[line ringing]

27:49.376 --> 27:50.502
[exhales sharply]

27:55.507 --> 27:58.426
[operator] The person you are trying
to reach is not available at this time.

27:58.510 --> 27:59.427
[scoffs]

28:06.142 --> 28:07.477
[sighs]

28:08.436 --> 28:11.147
[Ha-kyung] We're here
at Camp Site Letter B.

28:11.731 --> 28:13.525
So we need to go that way.

28:13.608 --> 28:15.068
Oh, that's a long walk.

28:15.735 --> 28:18.488
- Oh, it's no problem. Let's go.
- Okay.

28:19.864 --> 28:21.199
- [Ha-kyung] Can I help?
- [Si-woo] No, thanks.

28:21.282 --> 28:22.826
- [Ha-kyung] Are you sure?
- [Si-woo] Yeah.

28:22.909 --> 28:23.868
Let's go.

28:24.452 --> 28:26.496
I'll hop on. You're so strong.

28:26.579 --> 28:28.832
Are you riding it? Then I'll push.

28:28.915 --> 28:31.543
I'll make irrefutable evidence
when I confront them.

28:33.837 --> 28:35.755
Uh… Uh…

28:36.881 --> 28:37.882
Where is it?

28:38.550 --> 28:40.552
All right. I got time. I got time. Yeah.

28:44.556 --> 28:48.101
Ah!
[grumbles]

28:50.145 --> 28:51.146
What do I do?

28:56.693 --> 28:58.695
[snoring]

29:04.325 --> 29:08.163
[grunts, clears throat]

29:12.041 --> 29:14.169
[clears throat]

29:17.046 --> 29:21.718
[grunts]

29:22.844 --> 29:23.845
Hmm…

29:26.639 --> 29:29.976
[yawns]

29:31.853 --> 29:32.771
[light knocks]

29:33.396 --> 29:34.564
Did she go out?

29:35.815 --> 29:37.776
Si-woo, you had breakfast yet?

29:39.027 --> 29:41.654
Hmm. How about we go get, um…

29:43.907 --> 29:46.826
[sighs]
Where is everyone?

29:47.410 --> 29:48.453
[tongue clicks]

29:49.329 --> 29:50.497
[sighs]

29:50.580 --> 29:52.582
[light music]

30:00.298 --> 30:01.800
MOBILE DISASTER PREVENTION
AND WEATHER SYSTEM

30:01.883 --> 30:02.717
NO CONNECTION

30:09.057 --> 30:11.059
That's weird. I can't get a signal.

30:11.142 --> 30:12.602
Internet's not working?

30:13.186 --> 30:14.020
Yeah.

30:14.103 --> 30:16.272
They definitely said it would.

30:16.356 --> 30:18.483
It'd be great to at least see
the live reporting.

30:20.652 --> 30:21.945
Hang on a second.

30:22.028 --> 30:24.572
[line dials, rings]

30:24.656 --> 30:26.032
- [Seok-ho] Hey.
- Hello.

30:26.616 --> 30:29.327
Could you check
the current situation on the live radar?

30:29.911 --> 30:31.621
You can do it yourself.

30:32.997 --> 30:35.333
I'm outside and I don't have any internet.

30:36.084 --> 30:37.210
Just do it for a friend?

30:37.293 --> 30:38.878
[sighs]

30:38.962 --> 30:43.091
You have to be joking. Wait a second.

30:43.174 --> 30:44.008
What's…

30:44.092 --> 30:46.427
Oh, he's going over to…
Let me see your phone.

30:47.428 --> 30:52.809
Right now, the stationary front
is moving northward Jeju 5mm of rain.

30:52.892 --> 30:54.978
And it's barely drizzling
on the south coast.

30:55.061 --> 30:56.354
Okay.

30:57.689 --> 31:00.567
[Si-woo] It's drizzling in Jeju
and the southern region.

31:03.069 --> 31:04.320
[Si-woo] Just a second, Seok-ho.

31:04.904 --> 31:07.282
[Ha-kyung] Also ask
for the NWP model from 1:00 p.m.

31:07.365 --> 31:09.742
Oh, the NWP model too?

31:09.826 --> 31:11.327
[quirky music]

31:11.411 --> 31:12.662
Who are you with right now?

31:16.958 --> 31:18.710
With my girlfriend.

31:20.587 --> 31:22.422
[chuckles]

31:22.505 --> 31:26.342
Then forget about this stuff
and just enjoy your date.

31:26.968 --> 31:30.471
Team One's in the office, and I'll keep
an eye on the live situation.

31:30.555 --> 31:32.348
- [Seok-ho] I'm hanging up.
- Okay.

31:32.432 --> 31:33.391
[phone beeps]

31:36.644 --> 31:37.812
What did he say?

31:38.605 --> 31:43.484
He said there's lots of people at the KMA,
so I should focus on what I'm doing.

31:44.402 --> 31:46.571
I know that already. I'm just curious.

31:46.654 --> 31:48.072
[Si-woo] Seok-ho is right.

31:48.156 --> 31:50.700
We need to relax, so we can be rested.

31:50.783 --> 31:53.828
The stationary front
is heading north as expected.

31:53.912 --> 31:56.372
So just forget it.
Let's focus on each other.

31:57.624 --> 31:58.666
Okay.

32:00.668 --> 32:02.879
[water running]

32:02.962 --> 32:04.255
- [Si-woo] This, then?
- [Ha-kyung] Yeah.

32:15.934 --> 32:17.644
[breathing deeply]

32:20.521 --> 32:22.065
[sighs]

32:26.569 --> 32:27.695
Okay.

32:28.321 --> 32:29.364
Right.

32:29.989 --> 32:31.824
Team One will take care of it.

32:33.242 --> 32:35.244
Okay, forget it. All right.

32:43.002 --> 32:45.755
[Seok-ho] One vanilla latte, please.
Some soy milk, please.

32:45.838 --> 32:47.423
And just two pumps of syrup. No more.

32:47.507 --> 32:49.050
- [machine beeping]
- I'll use my free one.

32:49.634 --> 32:52.053
- What's your name?
- It's Shin Seok-ho.

32:57.392 --> 32:58.309
There's no card.

32:59.519 --> 33:01.854
What do you mean there's no card?
I just got my last…

33:02.438 --> 33:05.274
- From who?
- I don't know. A staff member.

33:05.358 --> 33:07.735
Yeah. I'm getting a coffee first.

33:07.819 --> 33:10.697
When our manager comes in,
she can check for you, okay?

33:10.780 --> 33:12.156
Can you just pay for it now?

33:12.740 --> 33:15.618
So you're saying
my punch card is lost now?

33:16.202 --> 33:18.913
I let you people keep it
because you said it would be safe.

33:21.207 --> 33:23.376
Oh, 1302?

33:24.919 --> 33:26.421
Other customers are waiting right now.

33:26.504 --> 33:28.464
Right, how about we check one more time?

33:37.598 --> 33:38.808
Hello.

33:38.891 --> 33:40.852
Oh, what brings you here?

33:42.020 --> 33:43.855
This is a coffee shop.
I'm here for coffee.

33:43.938 --> 33:44.897
Right.

33:44.981 --> 33:47.608
What about you? What… what's going on?

33:47.692 --> 33:48.735
[sighs]

33:48.818 --> 33:51.320
They lost my card
with all 12 stamps on it.

33:52.655 --> 33:54.282
The one they stored?

33:54.991 --> 33:59.746
As I was saying, he must understand
we can't confirm the stamps right now.

33:59.829 --> 34:02.415
I'll look into this
when my manager arrives, okay?

34:02.498 --> 34:04.000
So, please, for now, if you could pay--

34:04.083 --> 34:06.210
I didn't bring my wallet
because I had a full card.

34:07.003 --> 34:09.547
- So should I cancel your order, then?
- Ridiculous.

34:10.131 --> 34:12.258
- Here, you can put it on this one.
- No, you don't have to.

34:12.341 --> 34:14.427
I owe you from the other day.

34:15.344 --> 34:16.721
What's your order?

34:18.014 --> 34:22.143
A vanilla latte, some soy milk,
and just two pumps of syrup, no more.

34:23.186 --> 34:26.189
Ah! Okay, that. And I'll have
a cold, iced Americano, please.

34:26.272 --> 34:27.648
You can put his on here.

34:27.732 --> 34:28.858
[sighs]

34:29.442 --> 34:30.693
- Um…
- [machine beeping]

34:31.861 --> 34:35.073
So saying "cold, iced Americano,"
that's redundant, see,

34:35.156 --> 34:38.367
because if they make it with ice,
it has to be cold, so…

34:39.160 --> 34:40.495
[indistinct chatter]

34:40.578 --> 34:41.871
[sighs]

34:42.455 --> 34:45.208
- Don't you think that I'd know that?
- Right.

34:47.418 --> 34:49.128
- Oh, and thank you.
- Okay.

34:51.172 --> 34:52.340
Mm, thanks.

34:54.133 --> 34:55.343
Go ahead.

34:58.721 --> 35:01.933
- [woman] One chamomile tea, please.
- [machine beeps]

35:02.016 --> 35:04.977
[car engine rumbles]

35:10.358 --> 35:12.777
No, wait! Hold on! Hey!

35:12.860 --> 35:14.028
Hey, my car!

35:14.112 --> 35:15.613
My car! My car!

35:15.696 --> 35:18.658
[Ki-jun] Hey! Wait! Stop

35:19.784 --> 35:20.785
Hey!

35:27.917 --> 35:28.835
What?

35:29.836 --> 35:31.254
It's bothering me.

35:33.089 --> 35:34.549
[Si-woo] It will rain, right?

35:35.591 --> 35:36.843
Don't you think so?

35:37.510 --> 35:40.096
Of course. Look how gray the clouds are.

35:40.680 --> 35:41.889
It'll rain.

35:43.558 --> 35:44.642
[sharp exhale]

35:44.725 --> 35:46.727
[birds chirping]

35:49.272 --> 35:51.190
[quirky music]

35:52.525 --> 35:53.484
Hey.

35:58.322 --> 36:00.116
I know you're curious too.

36:01.033 --> 36:03.828
Well, then, let's try something.
Hand me your phone.

36:05.997 --> 36:09.542
Okay. Whoever takes their phone first
does the dishes.

36:11.335 --> 36:13.004
Sure, but…
[inhales deeply]

36:13.588 --> 36:15.923
…shouldn't we cook something
before we worry about the dishes?

36:16.799 --> 36:19.635
Camping requires barbecue.

36:19.719 --> 36:21.804
- All right. Yeah.
- [plastic rustling]

36:22.471 --> 36:24.473
- [Si-woo humming]
- What you got?

36:25.808 --> 36:26.893
Huh?

36:27.768 --> 36:30.855
- [rustling]
- Huh? What?

36:31.564 --> 36:32.690
Why, what is it?

36:35.318 --> 36:37.945
Meat. I definitely put it in here.

36:38.029 --> 36:39.155
[rustling]

36:45.411 --> 36:47.413
[playful music]

37:12.104 --> 37:13.648
- [Ha-kyung] It's okay.
- [sighs]

37:13.731 --> 37:15.816
Camping always needs kimchi-jjigae.

37:16.400 --> 37:17.944
We don't have anything for the broth.

37:19.654 --> 37:21.948
Should I go get some beef
from the store over there?

37:22.031 --> 37:24.033
All we need for kimchi-jjigae is kimchi.

37:24.116 --> 37:26.285
- [giggles]
- [birds chirping]

37:28.371 --> 37:30.122
[Ha-kyung] It's okay.

37:31.332 --> 37:34.335
["Melting" by Cheeze playing]

37:51.060 --> 37:53.521
- How is it, uh, looking?
- [Ha-kyung] It's okay.

37:53.604 --> 37:55.815
- Is it good?
- I don't know.

37:55.898 --> 37:57.233
I haven't tasted it.

37:57.900 --> 37:59.860
- Wow, you're good at this.
- Okay, try it.

37:59.944 --> 38:01.362
- Try it?
- Mm-hmm.

38:04.365 --> 38:05.366
Mmm.

38:05.449 --> 38:06.784
- Very good.
- Is it good?

38:06.867 --> 38:08.119
Here, try it.

38:11.289 --> 38:13.416
- Hmm?
- Wow, I think I'm a genius.

38:13.499 --> 38:16.210
- It's so good.
- Stay. Oh, oh, hold it.

38:16.294 --> 38:17.586
[chuckling]

38:17.670 --> 38:20.881
VEHICLES SUBJECT TO FINES AND TOWS

38:22.008 --> 38:23.134
[groans]

38:24.844 --> 38:26.846
[phone ringing]

38:26.929 --> 38:29.181
HONEY

38:30.224 --> 38:32.351
- [Ki-jun] Hey.
- Where are you?

38:33.686 --> 38:35.980
- Oh, uh, Yu-jin…
- I'll go straight to your mom's place.

38:36.063 --> 38:37.523
I'll see you there, okay?

38:37.606 --> 38:38.816
You have to hurry.

38:48.159 --> 38:50.161
[somber music]

39:10.473 --> 39:11.891
[Yu-jin] Where are you coming from?

39:13.267 --> 39:14.769
And why are you so ragged?

39:16.020 --> 39:17.605
It's a long story.

39:18.981 --> 39:20.649
Did you forget what day it was?

39:21.317 --> 39:23.110
Your mom's birthday.

39:23.194 --> 39:25.946
You're so… cold-hearted.

39:26.030 --> 39:27.323
"Your mom"? Really?

39:27.907 --> 39:29.367
She's your mother-in-law, okay?

39:29.450 --> 39:30.576
You should call her "Mom."

39:31.160 --> 39:33.913
She called two days ago to make sure
that we could have dinner with her.

39:34.789 --> 39:36.290
[Yu-jin] Where were you all day?

39:36.832 --> 39:38.751
Do you know how awkward
it was alone with her?

39:40.836 --> 39:42.630
Did she say something to you again?

39:43.214 --> 39:45.216
Okay, I asked where you were!

39:45.299 --> 39:47.676
I'm old enough to go places
without your permission.

39:48.386 --> 39:51.889
Come on. I had something important
I had to check out.

39:51.972 --> 39:53.474
- And now…
- [sighs]

39:53.557 --> 39:56.769
Please don't say
you saw Jin Ha-kyung again.

39:58.104 --> 39:59.021
[sighs]

39:59.105 --> 40:02.400
You said you couldn't believe
that Ha-kyung and that ass are dating.

40:02.483 --> 40:04.902
So she's just so important for you?

40:04.985 --> 40:07.238
So much so you forgot your mom's birthday?

40:08.906 --> 40:10.241
I don't know what to do.

40:10.324 --> 40:12.868
When I ended my engagement
with her and married you,

40:12.952 --> 40:14.620
do you know how much crap people gave me?

40:14.703 --> 40:17.415
They said I betrayed a woman
who'd stuck with me through thick and thin

40:17.498 --> 40:20.126
and that I'm a shameless cheat
who bailed at the last second.

40:20.709 --> 40:23.129
I had to go through all of that.

40:23.212 --> 40:26.173
I can't let her get away
with playing the victim

40:26.257 --> 40:28.717
when she's dating that bastard Lee Si-woo!

40:28.801 --> 40:29.760
[Yu-jin] Oppa.

40:29.844 --> 40:32.388
I really wish you'd focus on our problems.

40:32.471 --> 40:34.974
We have so much stuff
we need to fix together.

40:35.057 --> 40:36.600
I know.

40:36.684 --> 40:38.185
But I have to take care of this first

40:38.269 --> 40:40.604
before I can focus
on anything else, Yu-jin.

40:40.688 --> 40:41.856
So what will you do?

40:43.149 --> 40:44.608
Expose them to the whole world, huh?

40:44.692 --> 40:46.235
So what if I want to?

40:46.819 --> 40:47.736
[scoffs]

40:47.820 --> 40:49.155
You don't think

40:49.238 --> 40:51.115
that people will be talking about us too
if that got out?

40:51.198 --> 40:53.200
Why is it that you won't consider that?

40:53.284 --> 40:55.035
[sighs]

40:55.786 --> 40:56.704
[exhales sharply]

40:57.621 --> 40:59.039
[Yu-jin] Be honest.

40:59.123 --> 41:01.500
I think you not wanting her
to play the victim is a cover.

41:01.584 --> 41:04.295
Aren't you just jealous of them
now that they're going out?

41:06.297 --> 41:07.256
"Jealous"?

41:07.339 --> 41:09.049
[Ki-jun] Me? Of Lee Si-woo?

41:09.133 --> 41:10.676
Why would I be?

41:10.759 --> 41:12.470
You're the one who would know that.

41:17.183 --> 41:18.100
[sighs]

41:20.436 --> 41:21.479
I…

41:23.856 --> 41:26.358
[breathing heavily]

41:26.942 --> 41:29.445
[crickets chirping]

41:33.073 --> 41:34.283
[Ha-kyung] It's not raining.

41:36.243 --> 41:37.328
I know.

41:43.918 --> 41:45.377
It's not going to, is it?

41:48.297 --> 41:49.507
Probably not.

41:51.091 --> 41:52.301
What's the time?

41:55.429 --> 41:57.681
It's going on 8:21.

41:59.725 --> 42:00.935
We're screwed.

42:03.020 --> 42:04.939
[chuckles]
Cheers.

42:06.440 --> 42:07.441
[Si-woo] Cheers.

42:12.571 --> 42:15.616
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

42:15.699 --> 42:17.701
[pensive music]

42:23.958 --> 42:25.125
[sighs]

42:30.464 --> 42:31.715
Hmm…

42:38.013 --> 42:40.683
It's been over ten minutes
since the meeting started.

42:40.766 --> 42:43.018
- [shushes]
- Okay.

42:44.436 --> 42:47.523
I thought we saw the NWP
had moved northward.

42:48.357 --> 42:50.192
Hmm? Then why isn't it raining?

42:50.276 --> 42:52.444
The Okhotsk's anticyclone
is abnormally strong

42:52.528 --> 42:54.154
and the cold air
in the north isn't moving,

42:54.238 --> 42:56.991
so the northing of the stationary front
is being delayed.

42:57.866 --> 43:02.329
Isn't that the point that Mr. Um said
in our meeting before this, you know?

43:03.080 --> 43:04.248
[Seok-ho] Yeah.

43:09.086 --> 43:10.713
When is it going to rain?

43:10.796 --> 43:13.465
Right now, we're looking
at the start of next week.

43:13.549 --> 43:15.050
However, if this weather continues,

43:15.134 --> 43:17.720
we can't rule out the chance of it
taking even longer.

43:20.222 --> 43:21.724
[sighs]

43:22.433 --> 43:24.351
[breathes deeply]

43:24.435 --> 43:25.728
[Bong-chan] Okay, then.

43:26.312 --> 43:28.981
PR should distribute explanations
to the press

43:29.064 --> 43:30.941
about why the rain has been delayed.

43:31.025 --> 43:33.277
And forecasting…
[sighs]

43:33.360 --> 43:35.738
…should stay focused on the live charts.

43:35.821 --> 43:36.989
[all in unison] Yes, sir.

43:37.072 --> 43:41.285
Wouldn't it be better if we mention
the possibility of a drier rainy season?

43:41.869 --> 43:43.746
- "Drier rainy season"?
- [Ki-jun] Yes.

43:44.246 --> 43:47.625
We can't do that
when the stationary front is still active.

43:48.250 --> 43:51.128
Even if it just stays cloudy
but doesn't rain,

43:51.211 --> 43:53.756
I don't think it's right to just rush
an announcement like that

43:53.839 --> 43:55.633
when rainfall's still likely.

43:56.592 --> 43:57.509
[scoffs]

44:00.012 --> 44:03.140
Isn't hasty conclusions
what you love? What?

44:03.223 --> 44:05.726
Your special sense isn't working so well
right now?

44:07.561 --> 44:12.107
Those senses are based on data
and the flow of the weather.

44:12.191 --> 44:13.901
Either it's right or it's not.

44:13.984 --> 44:15.611
We can't publish vague warnings

44:15.694 --> 44:18.030
just because we're afraid
of the criticism.

44:18.113 --> 44:19.907
"Publish vague warnings"?

44:19.990 --> 44:21.575
Isn't that what you were saying?

44:22.326 --> 44:23.619
Issue a statement?

44:23.702 --> 44:25.412
[tense music]

44:27.581 --> 44:29.291
[indistinct murmuring]

44:29.917 --> 44:31.418
Please stop. Both of you.

44:31.502 --> 44:32.920
No, you go on.

44:33.003 --> 44:33.921
Huh?

44:34.880 --> 44:36.048
[Bong-chan] Please continue.

44:36.548 --> 44:38.926
Why don't you two gentlemen
debate it together?

44:39.009 --> 44:40.969
And then you can draw a joint conclusion.

44:41.053 --> 44:44.848
And we'll release the explanation material
to the news as a result of your findings.

44:45.432 --> 44:47.935
[Bong-chan] That would be great, right?
Right?

44:48.727 --> 44:49.937
Is there a problem?

44:51.063 --> 44:53.691
Uh, no, Director. We'll debate.

44:55.442 --> 44:57.444
[Bong-chan] Great. Carry on.

45:00.072 --> 45:01.365
[Bong-chan sighs]

45:03.742 --> 45:05.744
[indistinct chatter]

45:13.627 --> 45:14.920
Um, Director…

45:17.047 --> 45:18.882
I'm heading to that meeting.

45:18.966 --> 45:20.217
Will you survive?

45:20.926 --> 45:22.010
Yes.

45:23.762 --> 45:25.389
[chuckles]

45:26.056 --> 45:27.975
[phone ringing]

45:29.643 --> 45:32.271
[intriguing music]

45:33.897 --> 45:36.024
[breathes deeply]

45:40.195 --> 45:43.031
[tense music]

45:50.914 --> 45:54.209
[tense music]

46:00.007 --> 46:02.718
Let's start with analyzing
why the last forecast was wrong.

46:03.927 --> 46:05.846
I thought we were gonna work
on the reasons

46:05.929 --> 46:07.347
why the rainy season delay happened.

46:09.475 --> 46:12.019
I think we'd have to go back
to the forecast

46:12.102 --> 46:13.562
and find out what we missed,

46:13.645 --> 46:17.399
so we can explain the difference
between our prediction and what occurred.

46:21.570 --> 46:24.031
All right, sure. Where should we start?

46:26.950 --> 46:28.202
[remote beeps]

46:28.285 --> 46:29.786
[Ki-jun] In the first set of forecast,

46:29.870 --> 46:32.414
you predicted the stationary front
would cause a rainfall starting

46:32.498 --> 46:35.250
in the Jeju area and the rest
of the southern region.

46:35.334 --> 46:36.752
Where did this conclusion originate?

46:37.669 --> 46:41.006
Considering the gale
of 100 hectopascals north of the front,

46:41.590 --> 46:44.760
and how fast the North Pacific anticyclone
is expanding,

46:44.843 --> 46:47.179
there was a high chance
that rain clouds would follow.

46:51.683 --> 46:53.310
You think those two
are gonna take a while?

46:53.393 --> 46:55.020
Oh, yeah.

46:59.066 --> 47:02.277
Haven't you heard anything about why
the explanation's going on for so long?

47:02.361 --> 47:03.987
They want to expand it.

47:04.071 --> 47:06.031
[sighs]

47:08.867 --> 47:11.578
[breathing deeply]

47:13.789 --> 47:15.707
[Si-woo] Look, I'm right about this.

47:16.458 --> 47:19.836
If you look over here,
this area is too strong for it to rise.

47:19.920 --> 47:21.338
- Hey, Mr. Lee.
- I'm right.

47:21.421 --> 47:23.507
- And it's too warm…
- Listen to me.

47:23.590 --> 47:29.054
The reason this front can move up here
is because of this huge anticyclonic belt.

47:29.137 --> 47:31.098
That's why this can't go down.

47:31.682 --> 47:33.850
You're still missing this whole big one.

47:33.934 --> 47:35.310
Just look at this, will you?

47:35.394 --> 47:38.939
[inaudible]

47:39.022 --> 47:40.983
[techno music]

47:55.706 --> 47:58.000
[inaudible]

48:14.808 --> 48:16.268
- Hello.
- Hello.

48:16.351 --> 48:17.519
- Hello.
- Hello.

48:24.276 --> 48:25.277
Where is Forecaster Lee?

48:25.360 --> 48:27.154
Oh, he's…

48:27.237 --> 48:29.781
in the Spokesman's Office,
discussing the press release.

48:30.907 --> 48:33.744
I think he said he would send you
an email about your work today.

48:34.494 --> 48:35.621
Ah, here it is. Uh-huh.

48:36.204 --> 48:37.080
Okay.

48:40.167 --> 48:41.793
- Great work.
- You too.

48:41.877 --> 48:43.003
Great work.

48:43.920 --> 48:45.255
Hey, don't worry.

48:45.339 --> 48:47.883
- [automated voice] Door is closing.
- They're not gonna fight again.

48:48.925 --> 48:49.760
[Dong-han chuckles]

48:50.260 --> 48:51.678
Let's all go get some dinner.

48:51.762 --> 48:52.929
- Sure.
- Okay.

48:53.555 --> 48:56.016
- [Myung-ju] How about something cold?
- [Dong-han] Like what?

49:09.780 --> 49:11.698
So it was the wrong call to predict

49:11.782 --> 49:13.784
that the stationary front
would move northward

49:13.867 --> 49:16.536
based on the trough
in central-northern China and the gale.

49:16.620 --> 49:17.496
[pen thudding]

49:18.622 --> 49:21.833
Anyone would have come
to the same conclusions in the moment.

49:21.917 --> 49:26.088
Mr. Um's theory that the stationary front
would come down was reasonable.

49:26.171 --> 49:28.674
Still, the probability was low.

49:28.757 --> 49:31.343
You always say that you
go off your gut feelings.

49:31.426 --> 49:35.097
But then you blame it all on the data
when your forecast is bad.

49:35.180 --> 49:37.724
To me, that looks like
a pretty lame excuse.

49:39.685 --> 49:41.061
I wasn't sure.

49:43.814 --> 49:45.816
I couldn't risk it on feelings alone.

49:46.692 --> 49:49.152
'Cause too many people's lives
depended on us.

49:49.736 --> 49:50.946
Someone said that to me.

49:53.532 --> 49:55.867
[pensive music]

50:03.583 --> 50:06.712
Then tell me why are you going
and risking it all with Ha-kyung?

50:08.088 --> 50:11.049
She looks tough,
but she's a soft soul inside.

50:11.133 --> 50:13.427
The way I already hurt her
was painful enough.

50:13.927 --> 50:15.762
We should focus on the release.

50:15.846 --> 50:17.723
If you're seeing her because you have

50:17.806 --> 50:19.683
some negative feelings
about me or my wife…

50:22.018 --> 50:23.770
Stop, it's not too late.

50:25.564 --> 50:27.983
Ha-kyung doesn't do anything carelessly.

50:28.608 --> 50:32.154
If she really started something with you,
then she's being sincere.

50:32.738 --> 50:34.030
And if she gets hurt again,

50:34.781 --> 50:37.659
there's a chance she won't ever
be able to recover.

50:38.952 --> 50:41.997
Don't you think it's really
not your place to say so

50:42.080 --> 50:43.665
when you're the one that hurt her?

50:43.749 --> 50:45.000
I know that.

50:47.753 --> 50:49.796
I know I seriously hurt her.

50:49.880 --> 50:51.673
That's the reason I'm worried for her.

50:51.757 --> 50:53.800
[somber music]

51:01.016 --> 51:02.559
Don't worry about that, then.

51:03.185 --> 51:07.105
I'm also the type of person
who doesn't start things if I'm not sure.

51:19.117 --> 51:20.952
We can use this as the release.

51:23.830 --> 51:25.207
I'll be going now.

51:25.707 --> 51:28.043
[papers rustling]

51:29.586 --> 51:31.046
But you should know…

51:38.428 --> 51:40.180
See you next week, Seong-jun.

51:40.263 --> 51:41.473
[Seong-jun] Okay, good night.

51:46.561 --> 51:47.854
[button clicks]

52:02.077 --> 52:04.496
[uneasy music]

52:36.444 --> 52:37.988
[sighs]

52:55.797 --> 52:56.882
Why…

52:58.425 --> 53:00.302
did you break up with him?

53:02.762 --> 53:03.722
What?

53:03.805 --> 53:06.641
Honestly, even to me,
he seems like a good guy.

53:07.475 --> 53:08.643
[Ki-jun] No.

53:09.394 --> 53:10.812
Si-woo is a good guy.

53:11.396 --> 53:13.857
Why leave a guy like that
for someone like me?

53:16.401 --> 53:17.485
[book thuds]

53:18.069 --> 53:19.529
You really don't know?

53:20.113 --> 53:20.989
No.

53:23.033 --> 53:24.618
I'm asking because I really don't.

53:25.702 --> 53:26.953
You asked me for my hand.

53:30.665 --> 53:32.167
You were the first.

53:33.543 --> 53:36.463
You were the first guy
who wanted to marry me.

53:36.546 --> 53:39.215
Not just go out. You were.

53:40.717 --> 53:41.551
[chuckles]

53:43.762 --> 53:45.180
[sighs]
Too bad for you.

53:46.181 --> 53:49.976
The man you married is flat-out broke.

53:53.855 --> 53:55.941
That's why you won't register
our marriage.

53:56.650 --> 53:58.610
[breathes deeply]

54:00.612 --> 54:02.948
Why are you so twisted around?

54:03.031 --> 54:06.952
Do you really think I'd hold up filing
'cause of something like that?

54:07.535 --> 54:08.370
Well, what then?

54:08.453 --> 54:13.166
You never really focused on the issues
between the two of us once we got married.

54:13.917 --> 54:17.545
You were always so focused on what
others would think about all of it.

54:18.129 --> 54:22.008
And now, you're in a crisis because
Jin Ha-kyung might be dating Lee Si-woo

54:22.092 --> 54:24.594
so even now,
you're focused on someone else.

54:25.178 --> 54:28.598
How can I file it if I don't know
if you really love me anymore?

54:30.767 --> 54:31.893
I don't know where we are.

54:31.977 --> 54:34.062
Don't make some excuse about it.

54:35.397 --> 54:36.690
It's all the same thing.

54:37.273 --> 54:40.860
Oppa, stop running around all the time!
If you love me, focus!

54:46.658 --> 54:48.284
[sighs]

54:52.330 --> 54:53.832
[door opens]

54:53.915 --> 54:54.958
[door slams]

54:56.334 --> 54:57.544
[sighs]

55:02.924 --> 55:04.259
[door lock beeping]

55:09.097 --> 55:10.056
[door lock beeping]

55:13.810 --> 55:15.854
[Si-woo chuckles]
Oh.

55:16.646 --> 55:18.356
Did you and Ki-jun have a run-in again?

55:18.440 --> 55:19.441
[exhales]

55:21.026 --> 55:22.318
I want to do better.

55:22.402 --> 55:23.987
- What?
- Huh?

55:24.654 --> 55:26.114
The stationary front.

55:26.990 --> 55:29.534
- Let's analyze it again.
- Why?

55:29.617 --> 55:31.828
Is there an unusual signal or something?

55:31.911 --> 55:35.081
No, I discovered this when I was working
on the report with Director Han earlier.

55:35.165 --> 55:36.207
Here.

55:37.375 --> 55:40.045
The Okhotsk Sea air mass
that was abnormally developing

55:40.128 --> 55:41.671
isn't expanding anymore.

55:41.755 --> 55:43.798
And there's vapor coming in
from the southwest.

55:43.882 --> 55:47.761
Isn't it still too weak for
the North Pacific anticyclone to start?

55:47.844 --> 55:49.763
- What do you think?
- I agree with you.

55:50.388 --> 55:52.974
Uh, look at this part over here.

55:53.058 --> 55:55.935
The rain particles get stronger
as it rises, don't they?

55:56.519 --> 55:58.396
Hmm. I'm not so sure.

55:58.480 --> 56:01.149
If the anticyclone on the Okhotsk Sea
stops developing

56:01.232 --> 56:02.859
and vapor keeps coming in
from the southwest,

56:02.942 --> 56:05.278
the North Pacific anticyclone will expand.

56:05.361 --> 56:09.324
And if all that's true,
I'd say it's two days till rain.

56:10.784 --> 56:14.329
[light music]

56:21.878 --> 56:24.380
Let's go with Mr. Lee's thoughts
this time.

56:24.464 --> 56:27.008
It's true that the southwest
shows a lot of vapor right now.

56:28.009 --> 56:30.470
Well, okay, then. Okay.

56:30.553 --> 56:33.515
[chuckles]
Thank you for, uh, believing me.

56:36.017 --> 56:37.060
[sighs]

56:39.229 --> 56:42.023
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

56:45.068 --> 56:46.653
[birds chirping]

56:52.033 --> 56:54.035
[foreboding music]

57:00.166 --> 57:01.209
[sighs]

57:07.298 --> 57:11.386
THE KMA'S WEATHER FORECAST
IS WRONG AGAIN

57:15.640 --> 57:16.516
[sighs]

57:19.185 --> 57:21.563
THE FORECAST IS WRONG AGAIN
WHAT IS THE PROBLEM?

57:21.646 --> 57:24.941
[breathes deeply]

57:33.324 --> 57:35.660
The KMA's forecast was wrong yet again.

57:35.743 --> 57:37.078
Why do you think that is?

57:37.579 --> 57:41.875
Global warming's speeding up,
and we see this with El Niño and La Niña.

57:41.958 --> 57:44.586
And the variables of forecasting
grow more complicated.

57:44.669 --> 57:46.504
Could you please put that
in simpler terms?

57:47.505 --> 57:50.717
In short, the climate is a car
ignoring all traffic lights

57:50.800 --> 57:52.927
and we're trying to guess
which way it's going to go.

57:53.011 --> 57:54.637
[keyboards clacking]

57:55.847 --> 57:57.557
The reporters are loving this.

57:57.640 --> 58:01.644
Also, because no big stuff's happened
for a while.

58:01.728 --> 58:03.021
[Myung-ju] Poor Ms. Jin.

58:03.104 --> 58:05.732
She's been suffering
ever since they made her director.

58:06.774 --> 58:09.027
Nothing's working out for her.
[sighs]

58:11.237 --> 58:13.114
[somber music]

58:25.919 --> 58:27.295
[Ha-kyung] Aren't you tired?

58:30.882 --> 58:31.883
Let's go in now.

58:33.134 --> 58:34.219
[sighs]

58:34.302 --> 58:35.428
I'm sorry.

58:35.512 --> 58:37.388
I shouldn't have insisted.

58:39.432 --> 58:40.850
We wouldn't have gotten it wrong.

58:42.644 --> 58:44.395
You didn't get it wrong.

58:45.104 --> 58:47.315
And it's not like
Mr. Um and I were right either.

58:49.442 --> 58:52.153
You said it yourself.
Weather is a variability.

58:52.737 --> 58:56.616
One tiny factor sometimes gets
to change the whole scene.

58:57.575 --> 58:58.743
What are we gonna do?

59:01.329 --> 59:03.456
Take our licks as we were wrong.

59:07.752 --> 59:10.630
[keyboard clacking]

59:28.398 --> 59:29.649
THE KMA'S ERRONEOUS FORECAST

59:29.732 --> 59:34.612
[reporter] The KMA has forecast a rainfall
of 50 to 100mm an hour in Seoul, Gyeonggi,

59:34.696 --> 59:37.323
Yeongseo and Gangwon,
starting early this morning.

59:37.991 --> 59:41.536
But currently, most areas
are only cloudy with no rain.

59:41.619 --> 59:44.330
Although we did avoid
a rainy morning commute today,

59:44.414 --> 59:46.541
many are complaining that they are tired…

59:46.624 --> 59:49.627
Bo-mi, I have a bit
of a headache right now.

59:49.711 --> 59:50.962
- Can you…
- Okay.

59:51.588 --> 59:53.298
- The KMA's forecast was wrong yet again.
- Wait.

59:53.381 --> 59:54.924
[reporter] Why do you think that is?

59:57.135 --> 01:00:01.556
Global warming's speeding up,
and we see this with El Niño and La Niña.

01:00:01.639 --> 01:00:04.183
And the variables of forecasting
grow more complicated.

01:00:05.476 --> 01:00:08.980
In short, the climate
is a car ignoring all traffic lights

01:00:09.063 --> 01:00:11.316
and we're trying to guess
which way it's going to go.

01:00:11.399 --> 01:00:13.610
- That sounds like a very difficult task.
- You know that woman?

01:00:13.693 --> 01:00:15.320
- Yeah.
- Shouldn't your supercomputers

01:00:15.403 --> 01:00:17.363
with their vast amount of accumulated data

01:00:17.447 --> 01:00:19.782
be able to account
for all those variables?

01:00:24.037 --> 01:00:24.912
[reporter] Thank you.

01:00:36.424 --> 01:00:38.301
You said weather's harder to predict

01:00:38.384 --> 01:00:40.928
'cause climate change
has increased so rapidly of late.

01:00:41.679 --> 01:00:43.640
Shouldn't something be done about that?

01:00:44.432 --> 01:00:49.854
Well, that's the reason we have the NWP,
so we can have more predictive power.

01:00:49.937 --> 01:00:53.066
[exhales]
So there's no clear fix for it?

01:00:54.067 --> 01:00:55.693
Well, we'll try our very best.

01:00:58.112 --> 01:00:59.364
[Yu-jin] Trying is easy.

01:01:00.573 --> 01:01:02.867
What's hard is doing your job well.
[sighs]

01:01:03.910 --> 01:01:04.827
Is this over?

01:01:05.953 --> 01:01:07.914
- Yes.
- Well, thank you.

01:01:10.249 --> 01:01:11.959
I heard that you're dating Si-woo.

01:01:15.963 --> 01:01:18.716
Did Han Ki-jun say that?
I told him it's not the truth.

01:01:19.634 --> 01:01:21.803
[smacks lips]
Well, he is charming.

01:01:23.137 --> 01:01:24.931
[Yu-jin] Innocent but intelligent.

01:01:25.890 --> 01:01:29.394
He's penniless, but at least
he has some self-confidence.

01:01:30.645 --> 01:01:32.647
And he's not hard on the eyes either.

01:01:36.067 --> 01:01:37.694
Can I ask you a question?

01:01:39.987 --> 01:01:42.115
Why break up with such
a good man like Si-woo?

01:01:43.241 --> 01:01:46.285
Is it because of his father?

01:01:47.995 --> 01:01:48.871
[scoffs]

01:01:52.333 --> 01:01:53.793
You think you know everything, huh?

01:01:56.129 --> 01:02:00.383
Si-woo's father, I know he's sleazy.

01:02:01.551 --> 01:02:04.804
But not so bad
that I would break up with him for it.

01:02:06.556 --> 01:02:07.807
Then why…

01:02:09.976 --> 01:02:11.269
Si-woo oppa…

01:02:12.562 --> 01:02:13.771
doesn't want marriage.

01:02:14.439 --> 01:02:16.232
[dramatic music]

01:02:16.315 --> 01:02:20.361
He has no intention of marrying anyone.

01:02:24.198 --> 01:02:25.408
[button clicks]

01:02:32.999 --> 01:02:34.167
[Ki-jun] Oh, you should know.

01:02:34.250 --> 01:02:38.880
Ha-kyung doesn't date just anybody
unless there's a chance of marriage.

01:02:40.298 --> 01:02:42.216
You are aware of that, right?

01:02:44.469 --> 01:02:45.845
[sighs deeply]

01:02:50.099 --> 01:02:52.810
- [elevator dings]
- [automated voice] Door is opening.

01:02:53.644 --> 01:02:54.771
Going up.

01:02:57.315 --> 01:02:58.691
[button clicks]

01:02:58.775 --> 01:03:00.276
[Soo-ja] Uh, wait for me.

01:03:00.359 --> 01:03:01.611
- Oh!
- [button clicks]

01:03:02.320 --> 01:03:03.404
Hello.

01:03:12.538 --> 01:03:14.999
[Ha-kyung] The same way
flowers bloom in spring

01:03:15.082 --> 01:03:18.002
and the rainy season comes in summer,

01:03:18.628 --> 01:03:22.632
marriage always felt
like a natural progression for me.

01:03:24.801 --> 01:03:26.469
However, with climate change

01:03:26.552 --> 01:03:30.139
and the growing uncertainty
of weather forecasting nowadays…

01:03:30.223 --> 01:03:31.641
Si-woo oppa…

01:03:32.809 --> 01:03:34.101
doesn't want marriage.

01:03:36.646 --> 01:03:40.608
He has no intention of marrying anyone.

01:03:40.691 --> 01:03:44.529
[Ha-kyung] What really is natural
to us anymore?

01:03:45.488 --> 01:03:48.825
["Abnormal Climate" by Giriboy playing]

01:04:25.444 --> 01:04:27.738
[Ha-kyung] I hadn't considered it
really till now,

01:04:27.822 --> 01:04:30.116
not getting married after dating.

01:04:30.199 --> 01:04:32.702
Who are you? My daughter lives here.

01:04:32.785 --> 01:04:33.995
- Oh?
- Uh…

01:04:34.078 --> 01:04:36.122
All of you are living together
because of your work?

01:04:36.205 --> 01:04:38.875
[Soo-ja] In the elevator,
there was a man you were talking to.

01:04:38.958 --> 01:04:40.835
How exactly does he know you?

01:04:41.460 --> 01:04:42.503
Thanks.

01:04:42.587 --> 01:04:43.629
Are you an only child?

01:04:43.713 --> 01:04:44.672
Why are you asking me?

01:04:44.755 --> 01:04:45.840
What's with the temperature in Yeouido?

01:04:45.923 --> 01:04:48.926
Take it down now and put a blink up
on the weather portal.

01:04:49.010 --> 01:04:51.304
[Ki-jun] The error on the disaster
prevention portal,

01:04:51.387 --> 01:04:52.972
you tipped him off, didn't you?

01:04:53.681 --> 01:04:55.474
You should have submitted
a report to me right away!
